- decided_at: '2026-09-08T09:30:00+00:00'
  event: initial
  value: Formalize rigidity for frames whose `out` map is a BIJECTION, not merely a total injection as the paper's Definition of a frame allows.
  reason: The paper's proof of rigidity needs sigma^-1(E) to be a full Reiter extension, and two steps fail for a merely injective shift. (1) Cn does not commute with sigma^-1: every model of sigma^-1(X) must be the image under the pullback of a model of X, which needs the shift to be surjective on valuations. (2) In the stage construction a rule of S whose consequent lies outside the image of sigma has no preimage rule to fire, so the stagewise correspondence breaks -- this is precisely what the paper's clause 'groundedness is inherited stagewise by the same argument' skips over. No counterexample to the injective case was found; the argument simply does not reach it. The paper's own remark on the definable-c0 loophole identifies the bi-infinite (bijective) frame as the one carrying the content and notes that there the shift is a genuine automorphism, so the bijective case is the intended one.
